um", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Illinois enters the 2028 presidential race as a Democratic-leaning state with no incumbent on the ballot. The sitting Republican president is term-limited, so neither party carries an incumbency edge, and the state's six-point Democratic partisan lean sets the starting point. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available yet, so the state's fundamentals drive the outlook.\n\nRecent headlines center on Democratic positioning: Governor JB Pritzker is weighing a 2028 run, is aiding midterm Democrats through a $20 million group, and Illinois was left out of the party's early primary calendar. Juliana Stratton's primary victory in March keeps state Democrats organized. None of this changes the underlying lean; the Democratic nominee starts favored on fundamentals alone, with wide uncertainty until polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7608, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.746, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7069, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7035, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7139, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7158, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.714, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7198, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.727, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7103, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.733, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.709, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7437, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7147, "margin": 6.0}]}